\subsubsection{Problem Setting}
We consider the problem of auto-regressive language generation using a neural network, denoted by \( T(\cdot) = d_L \circ \cdots \circ d_1 \circ e(\cdot) \), and consisting of stacked decoder blocks \( d_l \) and an embedding layer \( e \). For NLG, we augment \( T \) with a classification head \( \sigma \). Consider an input sequence \( s_t = [x_{1:p}, y_{1:t}] \) consisting of the concatenation of a prompt \( x_{1:p} \) and a sequence of generated tokens \( y_{1:t} \) where \( x_k, y_k \in Y \), with \( Y \) denoting the vocabulary space. Sequences are generated auto-regressively by sampling the next token \( \hat{y}_{t+1} \) from the predicted probability distribution \( \hat{p}_{t+1} = \sigma(T(s_t)) \). In the field of efficient dynamic inference, the early exit method dynamically selects an exit layer \( L_E \), and executes layers \( \{d_l\}_{l \leq L_E} \). Thus, the network can be written as \( T_{EE}(\cdot) = d_{L_E} \circ \cdots \circ d_1 \circ e(\cdot) \). For layer skipping, the execution of each layer \( d_l \) is controlled by a binary variable \( G_l \), where \( G_l = 1 \) denotes executing layer \( l \). The layer skipping model output is then defined as \( T_{LS}(\cdot) = G_L d_L + (1 - G_L)I \circ \cdots \circ G_1 d_1 + (1 - G_1)I \circ e(\cdot) \), where \( I \) is the identity function. For each case, we define the computational cost \( c \) as the number of decoder layers executed, omitting the fixed costs of the embedding layer \( e(\cdot) \) and classification head \( \sigma(\cdot) \). For early exiting, \( c = L_E \), while \( c = \sum_{l=1}^{L} G_l \) for layer skipping. For all experiments, we only consider the computation performed on the autoregressively generated tokens \( y_{1:T} \), as is commonly done. The prompt is propagated through the full network since the prompt tokens can be efficiently processed once and in parallel and provide important context for NLG.


\subsection{Performance Control Early-Exiting}

Early exiting: if the model is confident at early layers, you exit at early layers. 


\textbf{Their selling point:} Larger models pruned via their early exiting to smaller models performs better than smaller models which have been trained from scratch.

Early exiting is an inference technique is an inference technique which allocates budget adaptively to test samples based on their perceived confidence (uncertainty at each layer).


The most common approach of early exiting is to track the model confidence at early layers.

\textbf{Performance control early exiting:} They introduce a post-hoc early exit approach to \textit{control accuracy} by having a classification head at every layer and returning confidence scores. They do not rely on a datapoints confidence. Rather, they use a calibration set and average the accuracies of samples with similar confidence levels, and perform accuracy thresholding. They collect a group of samples around a particular confidence level and compute the average accuracy on those samples. So, they have a mapping of what accuracies different ranges of model confidence will result in. They argue that accuracy is a better indicator of model performance than model confidence.

\textbf{Driving motivation: }An adaptive pruning algorithm which is able to keep the size of smaller models while maintaining the cost of larger models. The method must be advantageous for both performance and computational cost.

This provides better control over performance than confidence-based approaches.

\textbf{Early exiting and related works: } An inference optimization technique which adaptively allocates budget to samples based on their perceived difficulty. Existing methods evaluate confidence of predictions at each layer and determine whether its okay for the model to exit. \textcolor{blue}{So I assume this means there is a classification head at each layer? Additionally, a possible drawback of this is that confidence is a tricky mechanism to handle, relying on other factors such as confidence.} So this means a pre-determined threshold level is set and when this threshold is statisfied, the model stops processing the hidden state via additional layers and exits.

