\textcolor{red}{LayerDrop is an approach to train over-parameterized networks such that it is possible to extract any sub-network without a post-hoc pruning process. This method takes advantage of the plasticity of neural networks to learn models that are resilient to random pruning.}

Randomly dropping layers during pre-training to allow for efficient inference time pruning. Allows for pruning without the need for healing damage with finetuning and reduces performance loss. \textcolor{red}{If well-chosen groups of weights are dropped simultaneously, the resulting small sub-networks can be very efficient. In particular, we drop entire layers to extract shallow models at inference time.} It is agnostic to other methods and easy to implement.

This work used layer dropping for pre-training BERT encoder transformers.

Previous works have used layer dropping while training convolutional networks as a regularization method to reduce training time.


