\section{Appendix / supplemental material}


\subsection{Hyperparameters}

\subsubsection{Qwen0.5B - Wiki to Wiki}

When finetuning qwen 0.5B with LoRA trained for 50 epochs on 2000 samples of wikitext. A learning rate of $1e-5$, layer drop 0.2, l1 w 0.0001, r8, alpha 8, gradaccum 4 works best at the moment.



\subsubsection{Qwen0.5B - Nemo to Wiki to Wiki}

The same hyperparams used in wiki2wiki seem to work best here. The performance is competitive until 20 \% sparsity, but drops off after.


\subsubsection{Qwen0.5B - openwebtext}

The layer drop models don't seem to be performing as well. The nemotron finetuned code is working better here.


\subsubsection{Qwen0.5B - Nemotron Post Training}

The nemotron post trained model perform extremely well at lower levels of sparsity, but the performance doesnt keep up at higher levels of sparsity

